{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RKDxxy2xkNAwvJmeDVDkjv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 35,\n3\t \"title\": \"Detached/undocked DevTools is a blank/empty window\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\n43.1.1\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nmacOS\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nmacOS Sonoma 14.7.3\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\narm64 (including Apple Silicon)\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\n39.8.10\\n\\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\\n\\nI don't know how to test\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nOpening dev tools in `detach` or `undock` mode should show dev tools.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nOn any electron version newer than 39.8.10, dev tools in detach/undocked mode is a blank/empty window, nothing loads. Only downgrading to electron 39.8.10 fixes it.\\n\\n<img width=\\\"1265\\\" height=\\\"880\\\" alt=\\\"Image\\\" src=\\\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2785f3c4-cf9d-45e6-aeb3-b7e54ad1c805\\\" />\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\nWorth noting: This is happening for a frameless transparent window. Opening it in any mode besides `detach` or `undocked` works, but is not usable in this case (and overlay window w/ click-through transparency).\\n\\nAlso worth noting: disabling all extensions does not fix it either.\\n\\nScreenshot of 39.8.10 electron:\\n<img width=\\\"1265\\\" height=\\\"878\\